From e5e60d4883a9255110219a2b9f68db6caee39a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:16:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add feature indicator strip to the page heading
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Move the RF monitor status out of the header toolbar into a shared
strip beside the page title. Every chip uses one component
(indicator-strip.js/.css): a 32 px button with a 16 px line icon,
"Feature · State" label, semantic tone and a full accessible name.

Chips, in fixed order, all driven by existing state only:
- RF monitor: propagation monitor level (unchanged logic).
- RX log: receiving / not seen, shown only while connected.
- Map: active map source from corescope-ui.js (CoreScope, MeshMapper,
  Offline map, Fallback, Radio map).
- Alerts: shown only while quiet hours are active.
- Update: shown only when an update is available; checksum mismatch
  is an alert.

The strip stays on one row: calm chips drop labels first, then all
chips go icon-only. Overview keeps its title hidden but shows the
strip. The propagation live region is pinned so it adds no page
scroll. No radio commands are sent.

Tests: new indicator-strip.browser.test.cjs in test:browser, build
files and required features; propagation and header-control tests
updated for the new location. npm test 342/342; full test:browser
passes. Simulated browser results only; no physical-radio evidence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019jwdUNLdgFDTkdkrPTAK1B
