diff --git a/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md b/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
index e7fad10..6f19896 100644
--- a/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
+++ b/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
@@ -15,3 +15,15 @@ Validate representative Overview, Messages, Network, Contacts, Radio, Settings,
 Submenus are included at every depth: contact options, message actions, sidebar tools, terminal, discovery results, inbox/outbox, identity comparison, import/export, confirmation dialogs and expandable sections. nightlink-design.js adds matching decorative line icons to existing action buttons and dialog headers while preserving their DOM controls, accessible names and event handlers. Do not create a separate appearance for deeper menu levels.
 
 The main Radio landing page uses a live identity/status summary and three labeled groups of full-width action cards: device/setup, routes/discovery and observation/diagnostics. Keep export and hardware details in an expandable section. Reuse existing tool controls and preserve their state across navigation; opening this menu must not issue radio commands.
+
+## Feature indicator strip
+
+Feature status chips live in the page heading, to the right of the page title (`indicator-strip.js`, `indicator-strip.css`). Register new status indicators with `NightlinkIndicators.register(id,{feature,icon,onClick})`; do not add status buttons to the header toolbar.
+
+- Label: `Feature · State`. Feature is a short sentence-case noun (`RF monitor`, `RX log`, `Map`, `Alerts`, `Update`); State is short sentence case (`Normal`, `Learning`, `Possible opening`, `Not seen`, `Quiet hours`). No trailing punctuation.
+- Accessible name `Feature: State. Detail.`; the tooltip repeats it. Detail states what the status means or where to act.
+- Tone sets the colour only: `ok` (green icon), `info` (blue icon), `warn` (amber chip), `alert` (red chip), `off` (dimmed), `neutral`. Use `warn`/`alert` only for states that need attention.
+- Chip: 32 px high (28 px compact), 9 px corners, 12 px label, 16 px line icon, 8 px gaps. Fixed order: RF monitor, RX log, Map, Alerts, Update.
+- Hide a chip when it has nothing to report (for example no update available). Below 1100 px the feature word is dropped; below 860 px and in compact mode calm chips show the icon only, while `warn`/`alert` chips keep their text. The strip stays on one row: if chips still do not fit, calm chips drop their labels first, then every chip shows its icon only. The tone colour, accessible name and tooltip still carry the full status.
+- Chips never send radio commands. Animation follows reduced-motion settings.
+
